{'type': 'text', 'text': '### Incident Investigation Report: EVT-00001\n\n---\n\n### Executive Summary\nAn investigation into security event **EVT-00001** identified **SSH brute-force activity (SSH-Patator)** targeting destination IP `192.168.10.50` on port `22` (TCP) originating from source IP `172.16.0.1`. The activity occurred on **April 7, 2017, at 03:07:00 UTC**.\n\n---\n\n### Event Details (EVT-00001)\n\n* **Event ID:** EVT-00001\n* **Attack Type:** SSH-Patator (SSH Brute Force)\n* **Source IP:** `172.16.0.1`\n* **Destination IP:** `192.168.10.50`\n* **Protocol:** TCP (Protocol 6)\n* **Start / End Time:** `2017-04-07 03:07:00+00:00`\n* **Flow Count:** 2\n* **Mean Anomaly Score:** `0.02493` (Indicates high anomaly)\n* **Observed Target Ports:** Port `22` (SSH)\n\n---\n\n### Flow-Level Evidence\n\nTwo anomalous flows targeting port 22 were recorded during the event timeframe:\n\n1. **Flow ID:** `172.16.0.1-192.168.10.50-52038-22-6`\n   * **Connection:** `172.16.0.1:52038` → `192.168.10.50:22`\n   * **TCP Flags:** `PSH`\n   * **Packets (Fwd / Bwd):** 14 / 16\n   * **Anomaly Score:** `0.02439`\n   * **Label:** `SSH-Patator`\n\n2. **Flow ID:** `172.16.0.1-192.168.10.50-52036-22-6`\n   * **Connection:** `172.16.0.1:52036` → `192.168.10.50:22`\n   * **TCP Flags:** `PSH`\n   * **Packets (Fwd / Bwd):** 16 / 16\n   * **Anomaly Score:** `0.02547`\n   * **Label:** `SSH-Patator`\n\n---\n\n### Host Context & Host History\nHost `172.16.0.1` has a significant history of malicious/attack events involving `192.168.10.50` and other internal hosts across multiple attack categories (74 total events recorded), including:\n* **DoS / DDoS Attack Vectors:** DoS Hulk (31 events), DDoS (16 events), DoS Slowhttptest (4 events), DoS GoldenEye (2 events)\n* **Reconnaissance & Exploitation:** Heartbleed (7 events), PortScan (5 events), Web Attack - XSS (4 events)\n* **Credential Attacks:** FTP-Patator (2 events), SSH-Patator (1 event), Web Attack - Brute Force (1 event)\n\n---\n\n### Recommendations & Mitigations\n1. **Host Isolation / IP Blocking:** Temporarily block or restrict inbound traffic from `172.16.0.1` targeting sensitive internal network zones.\n2. **SSH Hardening on `192.168.10.50`:**\n   * Disable password authentication in favor of public key authentication.\n   * Implement rate limiting or install tools like `fail2ban` to block repeated failed SSH login attempts.\n3. **Log Review:** Inspect SSH login logs (`/var/log/auth.log` or `/var/log/secure`) on `192.168.10.50` to verify if any brute-force attempt resulted in a successful authentication.', 'extras': {'signature': ''}}